{
  "title": "More worry than enthusiasm about the idea of gene editing for babies",
  "x_axis": "% of U.S. adults who say the possibility of gene editing to give healthy babies a much reduced risk of serious diseases and conditions makes them ...",
  "y_axis": "Enthusiastic, Worried",
  "units": "",
  "ticks": ["Very", "Somewhat", "Not too", "Not at all"],
  "legend": {
    "Very": "#1f77b4",
    "Somewhat": "#ff7f0e",
    "Not too": "#2ca02c",
    "Not at all": "#9467bd"
  },
  "data_points": [
    {"Very": [15, 22], "Somewhat": [34, 46], "Not too": [30, 23], "Not at all": [19, 8]},
    {"Very": [15, 22], "Somewhat": [34, 46], "Not too": [30, 23], "Not at all": [19, 8]}
  ],
  "notes": "Respondents who did not give an answer are not shown.\nSource: Survey of U.S. adults conducted March 2-28, 2016.\n\"U.S. Public Wary of Biomedical Technologies to 'Enhance' Human Abilities\" Pew Research Center"
}
```

